ode3.katavasia:
Only the prayer of the Prophetess Hannah
unsealed the bonds of the barren womb
and stilled the unbearable taunts of the fertile woman;
for she offered up a broken spirit to the Lord,
the God of knowledge.

troparia.text:
The Virgin gave birth without the experience of those things that pertain to motherhood.
But though she was a mother, she remained a virgin;
wherefore praising her, we cry: Rejoice, O Theotokos.

ode5.irmos:
Rising early, we cry out to Thee, O Lord:
"Save us;
for Thou art our God;
we know no other but Thee!"

ode5.katavasia:
O children of the Church who appear as light,
receive the fiery dew of the Spirit,
the redeeming purification from your faults;
for now the Law has gone forth from Zion,
the Grace of the Spirit which appears as tongues of fire.

troparia.text:
Unto Him Who by His descent destroyed the adversary,
and Who by His ascent raised up mankind give praise;
O ye priests, hymn, and ye peoples, supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.

stichera.text:
Let us who are in the world keep festival like the Angels,
and to God Who is borne upon a throne of glory
let us sing this hymn aloud:
"Holy art Thou, heavenly Father;
Holy art Thou, coeternal Word;
Holy art Thou, All-holy Spirit."
